'''Mt Maunganui''' will be a future parliamentary [[New Zealand electorates|electorate]] in the [[2026 New Zealand general election]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |url= https://elections.nz/assets/pagecomponent-file-files/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2025-WEB.pdf |access-date=20 August 2025 |website=Electoral Commission |publisher=Electoral Commission}}</ref> The [[Tauranga (New Zealand electorate)|Tauranga]] electorate is moving westwards, with the [[Bay of Plenty (New Zealand electorate)|Bay of Plenty electorate]] gaining the suburb of [[Mount Maunganui]]. This shift triggered a renaming to Mt Maunganui. Also included are the suburbs of [[Papamoa]], [[Welcome Bay]], [[Hairini]], [[Maungatapu, Tauranga|Maungatapu]], [[Ohauiti]], [[Waimapu]], and [[Poike, New Zealand|Poike]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Conchie |first1=Sandra |title=Electorate boundary changes for BoP |url=https://www.sunlive.co.nz/news/370014-electorate-boundary-changes-for-bop.html |access-date=20 August 2025 |work=Sunlive |date=13 August 2025}}</ref> The electorate will be used from the next general election onwards.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Electorate boundaries finalised |url= https://elections.nz/media-and-news/2025/electorate-boundaries-finalised/ |access-date=15 August 2025 |website=Elections |language=en-NZ}}</ref>

==Election results==
===2026 election===
The [[2026 New Zealand general election|next election]] will be held on 7 November 2026. Candidates for Mt Maunganui are listed at ''[[Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate#Mt Maunganui|Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate § Mt Maunganui]]''. Official results will be available after 27 November 2026.<ref name="ge2026_dates">{{Cite web |last= |date=2026 |title=Key dates |url=https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260415030403/https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |archive-date=15 April 2026 |access-date=27 April 2026 |website=Vote NZ}}</ref>

